      statement: "A security guard walks her nightly round along the fence of a rectangular warehouse yard, starting at corner A and passing corners B, C and D before returning to A. The yard is 120 m long and 70 m wide. For the completed round, calculate (a) the distance the guard walks, (b) the guard's displacement.",
      solution: "(a) Distance is every metre actually walked — the whole perimeter. Work in letters first: S = a + b + a + b = 2(a + b). Only now put the numbers in: S = 2(120 + 70) = 380 m.\n(b) Displacement compares only the final and initial positions. The guard ends exactly where she started, so the change in position is zero: S_x = 0. No numbers were needed at all.",
