      concept: "Card-level synthesis: distance/displacement + average/instantaneous speed/velocity on a circular track",
      images: [], sketch: "cards/sketches/P10.svg", solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P10.svg", keyInfo: "circular track → trajectory: circle\none full lap → end = start\n300 m → L\nconstant speed → |v| = const\n100 s → T\nher average speed → find v_avg\nher average velocity for the full lap → find S_x/T\nher instantaneous velocity 50 s into the lap → find v at t = 50 s\nher displacement 25 s into the lap → find S_x at t = 25 s",
      statement: "A speed skater completes one full lap of a 300 m circular track at a constant speed, finishing the lap in 100 s. Calculate (a) her average speed, (b) her average velocity for the full lap, (c) her instantaneous velocity 50 s into the lap, (d) her displacement 25 s into the lap.",
      solution: "(a) Average speed = L/T = 300/100 = 3 m/s.\n(b) After a full lap she is back at the start, so S_x = 0 and average velocity = S_x/T = 0.\n(c) At t = T/2 = 50 s she is diametrically opposite the start. The speed is constant, so v = L/T = 3 m/s, but the tangent there points the other way: her velocity is opposite to her initial direction.\n(d) At t = T/4 = 25 s she has done a quarter lap. From L = 2πr: r = L/(2π). The displacement is the quarter-circle chord: S_x = r√2 = L/(π√2) = 300/(π√2) ≈ 67.5 m, at 45° to her initial direction.",
      answer: "(a) L/T = 3 m/s\n(b) 0\n(c) L/T = 3 m/s, opposite to initial direction\n(d) S_x = L/(π√2) ≈ 67.5 m, at 45° to initial direction",
      meaning: "Four sub-questions, four completely different kinds of answer: a plain number (a), a flat zero that hides all the effort (b), a number that needs a direction attached (c), and a number that needs geometry to find at all (d).",
      whatIf: "What if she'd skated the same lap at double the speed (T: 100 s → 50 s)? Look at the letter answers: everything with T in it changes — (a) and (c) double to 6 m/s. (d) changes too, because 25 s is now half a lap: the displacement becomes the diameter, 2r = L/π ≈ 95.5 m. Only (b) stays zero for the full lap. Speed changes the \"how,\" never the \"where you end up\" after a whole lap."
