      solution: "Speed is distance over time: v = S/t. Turn the units into metres and seconds first.\n(a) S = 200 **k**m = 200·10³ m = 200000 m  (k = kilo = 10³ — the prefix table is in M01, section 7).\nt = 90 min = 90·60 s = 5400 s  (1 min = 60 s).\nv = S/t = 200000/5400 ≈ 37 m/s.\nIt is an average speed: a real car speeds up, slows down and stops. 37 m/s is the steady speed that would cover the same 200 km in the same 90 min.\n(b) S = 1.5 **k**m = 1.5·10³ m = 1500 m.\nv = S/t = 1500/4.5 ≈ 333 m/s.\n(c) S = 6000 **k**m = 6000·10³ m = 6000000 m.\nt = 5 days = 5·24 h = 5·24·3600 s = 432000 s  (1 day = 24 h, 1 h = 3600 s).\nv = S/t = 6000000/432000 ≈ 13.9 m/s.",
