      images: [], sketch: "cards/sketches/P44.svg", solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P44.svg", keyInfo: "straight road → trajectory: line\nat 12 m/s → u_1\nthe next 5.0 s → Δt_1\nconstant acceleration of 0.80 m/s² → a_1\nslows down uniformly → a_2 = const, against the motion\n10 s later → Δt_2\n4.0 m/s → v_2\nFind the speed of the ambulance at the end of the first 5.0 s → find v_1\nFind the acceleration during the slowing-down stage → find a_2\nwhich way it points → find: direction of a_2",
      statement: "An ambulance leaves a junction on a straight road at 12 m/s. For the next 5.0 s it speeds up with a constant acceleration of 0.80 m/s². Then, approaching the hospital, the driver slows down uniformly so that 10 s later the ambulance is moving at 4.0 m/s.\n(a) Find the speed of the ambulance at the end of the first 5.0 s.\n(b) Find the acceleration during the slowing-down stage. Give its size and say which way it points.",
