      statement: "A passenger aircraft starts its take-off roll from rest and accelerates uniformly. A passenger's GPS app shows that it reaches 100 km/h after 16 s.\n(a) Find the acceleration, in m/s².\n(b) The aircraft must reach 250 km/h to take off. What is the shortest runway it needs? Give the answer to the nearest 100 m.",
      solution: "(a) First the speed in m/s (1 km/h = 1000 m / 3600 s):\nv_1 = 100·1000/3600 ≈ 27.8 m/s\na = (v_1 − u)/t_1 = 27.8/16 ≈ 1.74 m/s²\n(b) v_2 = 250·1000/3600 ≈ 69.4 m/s. Now we know u, v_2 and a; no time is given or asked — the formula without t:\nv_2² = u² + 2a·S, so S = (v_2² − u²)/(2a)\nS = 69.4²/(2·1.74) ≈ 4820/3.47 ≈ 1390 m ≈ 1400 m",
