      statement: "It starts to rain and your convertible is parked, roof down, 15 m from the garage. The keys are inside the house, so you push the car. Pushing, you can give it an acceleration of at most 2.0 m/s²; pulling back from the front, you can slow it at most at 3.0 m/s². The car must be at rest when it reaches the garage.\nWhat is the shortest time in which you can get the car into the garage?",
      solution: "The fastest plan (as in P56): speed up as hard as you can, then slow down as hard as you can, with no time in between. Call the top speed v.\nPushing from rest to v (no time given — the formula without t): S_1 = v²/(2a_1) = v²/4\nBraking from v to rest: S_2 = v²/(2|a_2|) = v²/6\nTogether they make the 15 m:\nv²/4 + v²/6 = 15\nv²·5/12 = 15, so v² = 36 and v = 6.0 m/s\nTimes: Δt_1 = v/a_1 = 6.0/2.0 = 3.0 s, Δt_2 = v/|a_2| = 6.0/3.0 = 2.0 s\nt_min = Δt_1 + Δt_2 = 5.0 s",
