      anchors: ["T03#coordinate-equation"],
      buildsOn: ["P66", "P68"], leadsTo: ["P110", "P112", "P70", "P72", "P84"],
      concept: "x(t) = x₀ + ux·t + ax·t²/2: the same parabola lifted to start at x₀",
      images: [], sketch: "cards/sketches/P69.svg", solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P69.svg", keyInfo: "positions are measured from the control tower → x = 0 at the tower\nx₀ = −75 m → x_0\nmoving towards it at 20 m/s → u_x = +20 m/s\nconstant acceleration of 2.0 m/s² → |a| = const\npointing back along the track → a_x < 0\nWrite the equation of motion x(t) → find x(t)\nFind x at t = 0, 10 s and 20 s → find x(0), x(10), x(20)\nsketch x(t) → draw x(t)\nAt what moments → find t\nlevel with the control tower → x = 0",
      statement: "On a straight test track, positions are measured from the control tower. At t = 0 a test vehicle is at x₀ = −75 m (75 m before the tower), moving towards it at 20 m/s. The engineers switch its motor to drive back towards the start, which gives it a constant acceleration of 2.0 m/s² pointing back along the track.\n(a) Write the equation of motion x(t).\n(b) Find x at t = 0, 10 s and 20 s, and sketch x(t) for the first 20 s.\n(c) At what moments is the vehicle level with the control tower?",
      solution: "(a) The axis points from the start towards the tower, so u_x = +20 m/s; the acceleration points back, so a_x = −2.0 m/s²; x_0 = −75 m (T03, section 8):\nx(t) = x_0 + u_x·t + a_x·t²/2 = −75 + 20t − t²\n(b) x(0) = −75 m\nx(10) = −75 + 200 − 100 = +25 m\nx(20) = −75 + 400 − 400 = −75 m\nA parabola opening downward: from −75 m up to +25 m at 10 s (where v_x = 20 − 2.0t = 0), and back to −75 m at 20 s.\n(c) Level with the tower means x = 0:\n−75 + 20t − t² = 0, so t² − 20t + 75 = 0, (t − 5)(t − 15) = 0\nt = 5.0 s and t = 15 s",
      answer: "(a) x = −75 + 20t − t²\n(b) x = −75 m, +25 m, −75 m; a parabola with its top at 25 m at 10 s\n(c) t = 5.0 s and t = 15 s",
      meaning: "The vehicle passes the tower twice: once going forward at 5.0 s, once coming back at 15 s. A displacement graph would never show this. Only the coordinate, which \"remembers\" where the tower is, tells you when the vehicle passes it.",
      whatIf: "What if you plotted the displacement S_x(t) = 20t − t² instead — would it answer (c)? No. It is the same parabola moved up by 75 m, and it crosses zero at 0 and 20 s — the moments the vehicle is back at its start, not at the tower. x_0 moves the curve and changes which questions it can answer."
