      solution: "(a) x_0 = 0, u_x = −6.0 m/s, a_x = +2.0 m/s²:\nx(t) = x_0 + u_x·t + a_x·t²/2 = −6.0t + t²\n(b) x = 16: t² − 6.0t = 16, so t² − 6t − 16 = 0, (t − 8)(t + 2) = 0\nt = −2 s is before the shove — not part of this motion. So t = 8.0 s.\n(c) First the cart moves in the −x direction and slows down:\nv_x = u_x + a_x·t = −6.0 + 2.0t = 0 at t = 3.0 s\nx(3.0) = −6.0·3.0 + 3.0² = −18 + 9 = −9.0 m\nThen the fan drives it back: through 0 at t = 6.0 s, on to 16 m at 8.0 s.",
