      images: [], sketch: "cards/sketches/P86.svg", solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P86.svg", keyInfo: "aims her dart gun horizontally → u_y = 0\nstraight at the monkey → aimed at the same height\n25 m away → d\n50 m/s → u_x\nAt the instant of the shot → same t = 0\nlets go of the branch → monkey: u = 0\nTake g = 9.8 m/s² → g\nignore air resistance → a = g, down\nHow long does the dart take to cover the 25 m horizontally → find t\nHow far does the dart drop → find h_dart\nHow far does the monkey drop → find h_monkey\nDoes the dart hit the monkey → compare",
      statement: "A monkey at a zoo has got tangled in some wires and hangs from a branch. To free it safely, a vet must put it to sleep with a sedative dart. She aims her dart gun horizontally, straight at the monkey, which is 25 m away. The dart leaves the gun at 50 m/s. At the instant of the shot the startled monkey lets go of the branch. Take g = 9.8 m/s² and ignore air resistance.\n(a) How long does the dart take to cover the 25 m horizontally?\n(b) How far does the dart drop in that time? How far does the monkey drop?\n(c) Does the dart hit the monkey?",
      solution: "(a) Horizontally the dart keeps a constant 50 m/s: t = d/u_x = 25/50 = 0.50 s\n(b) The dart starts with u_y = 0, so it drops h = g·t²/2 = 9.8·0.50²/2 ≈ 1.2 m.\nThe monkey starts falling from rest at the same moment, with the same g: the same 1.2 m.\n(c) Yes. Both start at the same height and fall by the same amount in the same time, so when the dart reaches the monkey's line they are at the same height.",
      answer: "(a) t = d/u_x = 0.50 s\n(b) both drop h = g·t²/2 ≈ 1.2 m\n(c) yes, it hits",
      meaning: "Letting go was the monkey's worst move. Had it held on, the dart would have passed 1.2 m below it. Gravity pulls the dart and the monkey down together, so relative to each other they move as if gravity did not exist — in a straight line along the aim. (Compare the icicle drops in P80.)",
      whatIf: "What if the vet stood lower and aimed upwards, straight at the monkey — would it still work? Yes. Without gravity the dart would fly along the aim line and hit; with gravity both dart and monkey fall the same g·t²/2 below where they would have been. As long as the dart reaches the monkey before they hit the ground, it hits."
