      solution: "(a) x grows by 6 m every 0.20 s: u_x = Δx/Δt = 6/0.20 = 30 m/s\n(b) The ball is highest at t = 1.0 s (the y values are symmetric about it). There v_y = 0, so u_y = g·t_top = g·1.0.\nThe greatest height: H = u_y²/(2g) = (g·1.0)²/(2g) = g/2 = 10.0 m, so g = 20 m/s² and u_y = 20 m/s.\nCheck: y(0.2) = u_y·t − g·t²/2 = 20·0.2 − 10·0.2² = 4.0 − 0.4 = 3.6 m — as in the table.\n(c) tan α = u_y/u_x = 20/30, so α ≈ 34°\n(d) With g' = 40 m/s² and the same launch:\nt_top = u_y/g' = 0.50 s, so the flight time is 1.0 s\nH' = u_y²/(2g') = 20²/80 = 5.0 m\nR' = u_x·t = 30·1.0 = 30 m",
