      meaning: "The vertical motion uses only uy and decides the time; the horizontal motion uses only ux and turns that time into distance. The two only meet through t.",
      whatIf: "What if she threw at the same speed but at 60° — would the ball land further away? No — at the same 35 m. Now u_y ≈ 17.3 m/s and u_x = 10 m/s: the ball goes three times higher (15 m) and stays up 1.7 times longer (3.5 s), but lands at the same point. Complementary angles share the range (T04, section 7)."
