      solution: "u_x = u_y = u·cos 45° = 16·0.707 ≈ 11.3 m/s\n(a) t_top = u_y/g = 11.3/9.8 ≈ 1.15 s; the flight lasts t = 2t_top ≈ 2.3 s\n(b) R = u_x·t = 11.3·2.31 ≈ 26 m\n(c) H = u_y²/(2g) = 11.3²/(2·9.8) ≈ 6.5 m\n(d) Both u_x and u_y grow by 5 %, so the flight time and the horizontal speed both grow by 5 %. R = u_x·t grows by 1.05·1.05 ≈ 1.10, about 10 %: R' ≈ 28.8 m, some 2.7 m farther.",
