      statement: "In 1971 the Apollo 14 astronaut Alan Shepard hit golf balls on the Moon, where g ≈ 1.6 m/s² (about one sixth of Earth's 9.8 m/s²) and there is no air.\n(a) A ball leaves the club at 30 m/s, 45° above the horizontal. Find its flight time, greatest height and range on level ground on Earth (ignore air) and on the Moon.\n(b) Without calculating, by what factor does each of the three change when g is divided by 6? Explain.",
