      statement: "A body moves along the x-axis according to x = 12 + 10t − 2t² (SI units).\n(a) When does it change direction?\n(b) Where is it at that moment?\n(c) When does it come back to where it started?\n(d) When does it pass the origin, x = 0?",
      solution: "Compare with x = x_0 + u_x·t + a_x·t²/2: x_0 = 12 m, u_x = 10 m/s, a_x/2 = −2, so a_x = −4 m/s².\nv_x = u_x + a_x·t = 10 − 4t\n(a) The direction changes when v_x passes through zero: t = 10/4 = 2.5 s\n(b) x(2.5) = 12 + 10·2.5 − 2·2.5² = 12 + 25 − 12.5 = 24.5 m\n(c) Back at x = 12 m: 10t − 2t² = 0, so t·(10 − 2t) = 0: t = 0 or t = 5.0 s. So at 5.0 s — twice the turnaround time.\n(d) x = 0: 12 + 10t − 2t² = 0, so t² − 5t − 6 = 0, (t − 6)(t + 1) = 0\nt = 6.0 s (t = −1 s is before we started watching)",
