      statement: "A cyclist rides along a straight road, the x-axis. At t = 0 she is at x = −5 m. The graph shows her velocity vₓ against time t.\n(a) Where is the cyclist at t = 4 s?\n(b) Check your answer with the equation of motion.",
      solution: "(a) The area under v_x(t) is the displacement, not the position.\nFrom 0 to 4 s the area is a trapezium (read v_x(0) = 2 m/s, v_x(4) = 10 m/s):\nΔx = (2 + 10)/2 · 4 = 24 m\nThe start comes from outside the graph:\nx = x_0 + Δx = −5 + 24 = 19 m\n(b) The slope gives a_x = (10 − 2)/4 = 2 m/s². The equation of motion (T03, section 8):\nx(t) = x_0 + u_x·t + a_x·t²/2 = −5 + 2t + t²\nx(4) = −5 + 8 + 16 = 19 m — the same.",
