      images: [], solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P113.svg", keyInfo: "starts from rest → u = 0\nstraight road → trajectory: line\n+2.0 m/s² → a_1\nfor the first 10 s → Δt_1\n−2.0 m/s² → a_2\nfor the next 10 s → Δt_2\nSketch v(t) → draw v(t)\nHow far does the car travel between t = 10 s and t = 15 s → find S from t = 10 s to t = 15 s\nHow far does it travel in the whole 20 s → find S_tot",
      statement: "A car starts from rest on a straight road. Its acceleration is +2.0 m/s² for the first 10 s and −2.0 m/s² for the next 10 s.\n(a) Sketch v(t) for the 20 s.\n(b) How far does the car travel between t = 10 s and t = 15 s?\n(c) How far does it travel in the whole 20 s?",
      solution: "(a) First 10 s: v grows by 2.0 m/s every second, from 0 to v_1 = u + a_1·Δt_1 = 0 + 2.0·10 = 20 m/s.\nNext 10 s: v falls at the same rate, from 20 m/s back to v = 20 − 2.0·10 = 0.\nA symmetric \"roof\" with its top at 20 m/s at t = 10 s.\n(b) The distance is the area under v(t). At t = 10 s v = 20 m/s; at t = 15 s v = 20 − 2.0·5 = 10 m/s.\nThe area is a trapezium: S = (20 + 10)/2 · 5 = 75 m\n(c) The whole area is a triangle with base 20 s and height 20 m/s:\nS_tot = 20·20/2 = 200 m",
      answer: "(a) a triangle: from 0 up to 20 m/s at 10 s, back to 0 at 20 s\n(b) S = area of the trapezium = 75 m\n(c) S_tot = area of the triangle = 200 m",
      meaning: "A negative acceleration in the second half does not mean the car goes backwards. It is still moving forward, just more and more slowly, and stops exactly at 20 s. The a(t) graph tells you how v changes, not which way the car goes.",
      whatIf: "What if the negative stage lasted 15 s instead of 10 — what would happen after t = 20 s? The car would stop at 20 s and then move backwards for 5 s, reaching −10 m/s. From that moment the distance travelled and the displacement are no longer equal."
