      images: [], sketch: "cards/sketches/P114.svg", figure: "cards/figures/P114.svg", solutionFig: "cards/solutions/P114.svg", keyInfo: "at the same moment → same t = 0\ntowards each other → + and −\nstraight road → trajectory: line\nconstant speeds → |v| = const\n15 m/s → v_1\nFind the speed of the second car → find v_2\nWhat happens at 60 min → explain",
      statement: "Two cars leave two cities at the same moment and drive towards each other along a straight road at constant speeds. The graph shows the distance between them against time. The first car drives at 15 m/s.\n(a) Find the speed of the second car.\n(b) What happens at 60 min, and why does the graph go up again afterwards instead of continuing below zero?",
      solution: "Careful: this graph shows the distance d between the cars, not the position of either of them. Its slope tells how fast the gap changes.\n(a) Read off the graph: the gap d_0 = 144 **k**m = 144·10³ m (k = kilo = 10³ — the prefix table is in M01, section 7) shrinks to zero in t_m = 60 min = 60·60 s = 3600 s (1 min = 60 s).\nThe gap closes at d_0/t_m = 144000/3600 = 40 m/s.\nWhy that is v_1 + v_2: put car 1 at x = 0 and car 2 at x = d_0 (T02, section 4):\nx_1 = v_1·t\nx_2 = d_0 − v_2·t\nx_2 − x_1 = d_0 − (v_1 + v_2)·t\nEvery second car 1 closes v_1 of the gap and car 2 closes v_2. So v_1 + v_2 = d_0/t_m and\nv_2 = d_0/t_m − v_1 = 40 − 15 = 25 m/s\n(b) At 60 min the gap is zero: the cars meet and pass each other. After that x_2 − x_1 becomes negative, but a distance is never negative — d = |x_2 − x_1| — so the graph turns up, and the gap grows again at the same 40 m/s.",
      answer: "(a) v_2 = d_0/t_m − v_1 = 25 m/s\n(b) at 60 min the cars meet and pass; d = |x_2 − x_1| cannot be negative, so it grows again at v_1 + v_2",
      meaning: "On this graph the slope is not the speed of either car — it is how fast the gap changes, the sum of their speeds. A graph of x_2 − x_1 would go straight through zero and continue below it; the V shape appears only because a distance has no sign.",
      whatIf: "What if the cars drove in the same direction, the faster one behind — how long would the 144 km gap take to close? It closes at the difference of the speeds, v_2 − v_1 = 25 − 15 = 10 m/s, so t = d_0/(v_2 − v_1) = 144000/10 = 14400 s = 4 h."
