      statement: "A boy throws a ball towards a wall. The ball leaves his hand 1.5 m above the ground and 9.8 m from the wall, with a velocity at 35° above the horizontal. Air resistance is negligible. The diagram shows the first part of the ball's path; P is a point on the path.\n(a) Draw arrows to show (i) the velocity of the ball at P, labelled v; (ii) the acceleration of the ball at P, labelled a.\nThe ball takes 1.0 s to reach the wall. The initial speed of the ball is 12 m/s.\n(b) Determine the height above the ground at which the ball hits the wall.",
