      whatIf: "What if someone said \"the acceleration is negative only after the trolley starts moving backwards\" — is that right? No. From 8 s on the acceleration is negative while the trolley still moves forwards: it is slowing down. Negative a means \"the velocity is getting more negative\", not \"moving backwards\"."
