      solution: "Second law (entropy form, B4.4): ΔS_tot ≥ 0\n\"> 0\" for every real (irreversible) process, \"= 0\" only for an ideal reversible one.\nB — no: for a reversible process ΔS_tot = 0, so \"increases in every process\" is too strong.\nD — no: ΔS = Q/T — the same heat changes the entropy differently at different temperatures.\nA — no: the entropy itself is not zero; and its change is zero only for reversible processes.\nC — yes: \"never decreases\" covers both \"> 0\" and \"= 0\".",
