      whatIf: "What if the gas were heated from 0 °C — to what temperature must it go for the internal energy to really double? From 273 K to 546 K, which is 273 °C. On the Celsius scale \"twice 0 °C\" would still be 0 °C — a clear sign that the scale cannot be used for ratios."
