      statement: "During one stroke of a compressor, 250 J of work is done on the gas in the cylinder. In the same time 90 J of thermal energy leaves the gas through the cylinder walls.\n(a) Calculate the change in internal energy of the gas.\n(b) State whether the gas gets hotter or colder.",
      solution: "First law: Q = ΔU + W, with Q — heat given to the gas, W — work done by the gas (B4.1, section 4).\nTranslate the words into signs first. Work is done ON the gas: W = −250 J. Heat LEAVES the gas: Q = −90 J.\n(a) ΔU = Q − W = −90 − (−250) = −90 + 250 = +160 J\n(b) ΔU > 0, and the internal energy of a gas follows its temperature — the gas gets hotter.",
