      statement: "(a) Mia, of mass 72 kg, stands in a lift. The lift is moving upwards at a speed of 3.0 m s⁻¹ and comes to rest 2.0 s later. Calculate the reaction force on Mia from the lift floor while the lift comes to rest. [4]\n(b) Mia then travels in the same lift going downwards at the same speed, and it again comes to rest in the same time. Calculate the reaction force on Mia from the lift floor while the lift comes to rest. [3]\n(c) Hence, deduce which slowing-down period of the lift would make Mia feel:\n(i) lighter [1]\n(ii) heavier. [1]\n(d) In a serious stroke of bad luck, the lift cable snaps and the lift falls freely. Mia experiences a sense of weightlessness. Explain, using appropriate laws of motion, why Mia feels weightless in this situation. [3]",
