      solution: "Total momentum before is zero, so after: p₁ + p₂ = 0 → p₁ = −p₂ → p₁/p₂ = −1.\nKinetic energy in terms of momentum: E_k = ½mv² = p²/(2m).\nBoth pieces have the same size of momentum p, so E_k ∝ 1/m:\nE₁/E₂ = M/(2M) = 1/2\n(Check with speeds: the 2M piece moves at half the speed of the M piece.)",
      answer: "C (E₁/E₂ = 1/2, p₁/p₂ = −1)",
      meaning: "In an explosion momentum is shared equally (and oppositely), but energy is not: the light piece gets the larger share. That is why a rifle's bullet does the damage, not its recoil.",
