      statement: "(a) Asel and Bora are two skaters, initially at rest on smooth ice. They face each other, and Asel is holding a ball. Asel throws the ball to Bora, who catches it. The ball leaves Asel at 8.0 m s⁻¹, measured relative to the ground.\nThe following data are available.\nMass of Asel = 55 kg\nMass of Bora = 65 kg\nMass of ball = 3.0 kg\n(i) Calculate the velocity v of Asel relative to the ground just after she throws the ball. [3]\n(ii) State the direction in which Asel moves after she throws the ball. [1]\n(b) Calculate the speed V of Bora relative to the ground just after she catches the ball. Assume the speed of the ball stays constant during its flight. [4]\n(c) Determine whether Bora catching the ball is an elastic or an inelastic collision. [3]\n(d) Bora decides to wear padded gloves, like the gloves worn by cricket players who catch fast balls. Explain why padded gloves would protect Bora's hands when she catches the ball. [2]",
