      statement: "(a) A car moves with uniform circular motion and experiences a centripetal force.\n(i) Describe centripetal force. [3]\n(ii) State the type of force that provides the centripetal force on the car. [1]\n(b) The car has a mass of 600 kg and drives round a roundabout at a linear speed of 10 m s⁻¹. The radius of the roundabout is 15 m. Determine the centripetal force on the car. [2]\n(c) The car moves on to another roundabout, of radius 25 m. Its angular speed at this roundabout is 0.25 rad s⁻¹. Calculate the centripetal acceleration of the car at this roundabout. [3]\n(d) At this second roundabout, the car moves at the greatest speed possible before it would skid. The coefficient of static friction then satisfies μ_s = ω²r/g, where ω is the angular speed, r is the radius of the roundabout and g is the acceleration due to gravity. Determine the coefficient of static friction between the tyres and the road. [2]",
