      concept: "Elastic head-on collision with zero total momentum: both bodies bounce back with their original speeds",
      images: [], figures: ["cards/figures/A2-P058_1.svg"], keyInfo: "frictionless horizontal track → momentum conserved\nmass m and 3m → m_P = m, m_Q = 3m\nspeeds 3v and v → u_P = +3v, u_Q = −v\ncollide elastically → E_k conserved too\nWhich statement correctly describes the motion of P and Q after the collision → check each option against both laws",
      statement: "Two trolleys, P and Q, of mass m and 3m move towards each other on a frictionless horizontal track with speeds 3v and v as shown. They collide elastically.\n[Figure 1]\nWhich statement correctly describes the motion of P and Q after the collision?\nA. P and Q both stop.\nB. P moves to the left and Q stops.\nC. P moves to the left and Q moves to the right.\nD. P and Q both move to the left with different speeds.",
      solution: "Total momentum before: m·3v + 3m·(−v) = 0.\nTotal kinetic energy before: ½·m·(3v)² + ½·3m·v² = 4.5mv² + 1.5mv² = 6mv².\nA — momentum 0 ✓, but E_k = 0: not elastic ✗.\nB — Q at rest and P moving: total momentum ≠ 0 ✗.\nC — P back to the left at 3v, Q back to the right at v: momentum m·(−3v) + 3m·v = 0 ✓; E_k = 6mv² ✓.\nD — both moving left: total momentum negative ✗.",
