      statement: "(a) The arrangement shown below is used in a sports lab to test bat heads.\n[Figure 1]\nThe arm is pivoted, and the centre of mass of the test head is raised by a height h before it is released. The head then swings back to the vertical position, where it hits a ball. Calculate the maximum speed of the test head when h = 60 cm. [3]\n(b) Explain why, in reality, the speed of the ball will not be the same as the maximum speed of the test head. [3]\n(c) Another test is carried out with an arm of length 1.20 m, which is pulled back to 45° from the vertical, as shown.\n[Figure 2]\nCalculate the maximum speed this test head reaches just before it hits the ball. [3]",
